From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:42:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64_ilp32: name the personality "32"

With a single personality the designator defaults to
STRINGIFY_VAL(__WORDSIZE), but musl defines __WORDSIZE only in
<sys/reg.h>, so the designator was the string "__WORDSIZE" and
qualifications such as -e trace=getcwd@32 were refused.

Found by the test suite: options-syntax, filtering_syscall-syntax and
trace_personality_{,number_,regex_,statfs_}32.
---
 src/linux/aarch64_ilp32/arch_defs_.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/linux/aarch64_ilp32/arch_defs_.h b/src/linux/aarch64_ilp32/arch_defs_.h
index 3f4d0a1..6beb0d8 100644
--- a/src/linux/aarch64_ilp32/arch_defs_.h
+++ b/src/linux/aarch64_ilp32/arch_defs_.h
@@ -10,3 +10,9 @@
  * Only ILP32 tracees are supported by an ILP32 strace.
  */
 #define PERSONALITY0_AUDIT_ARCH { AUDIT_ARCH_AARCH64ILP32, 0 }
+/*
+ * The default designator is STRINGIFY_VAL(__WORDSIZE), but musl defines
+ * __WORDSIZE only in <sys/reg.h>, so it would be the string "__WORDSIZE"
+ * and "-e trace=getcwd@32" would be refused.
+ */
+#define PERSONALITY_DESIGNATORS { "32" }
